implementationPlan.description:
NO VALUE IS EVER RENDERED OR RETAINED (DoD 2) — the row's central arm, in the screen's test file. This is the leak the screen invites, so test it as an attacker would.

Submit a distinctive sentinel value through the set dialog, then assert that sentinel appears NOWHERE, across every state:
(a) after a SUCCESSFUL submit — in the rendered output, in the table, in the fingerprint cell;
(b) after a FAILED submit — THIS IS THE ONE. Echoing the typed value back so the operator can correct it is the natural, helpful-looking behaviour, and it is exactly how a secret reaches a screenshot. Assert the input is NOT repopulated and the sentinel is not in the DOM;
(c) in every refusal message (step 5 covers the codes; this arm covers the value);
(d) in any component prop a browser devtools inspector would show — assert against the rendered tree, not only the visible text, since a value passed as a prop is visible in devtools even when nothing paints it.

Search the WHOLE rendered container for the sentinel, not a specific node: an assertion scoped to the input misses the value re-rendered somewhere else.

MUTATE AND CONFIRM RED: make the failed-submit path repopulate the input, run the arm, confirm it goes RED, restore. A leak test that has never been seen red is not evidence — and this is the one arm on this row whose silent failure has a real-world cost.

Use a sentinel that cannot occur naturally, and do NOT commit a realistic-looking secret as a fixture (epic rail 3 forbids a secret in a committed fixture, and a plausible one invites a credential scanner alert).
